diff --git a/runtime/assets/texture_packs/README.txt b/runtime/assets/texture_packs/README.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..049efd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/assets/texture_packs/README.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Punch-Out!! controller texture packs: the game's Wii Remote art swapped for controller art.
+Copy one folder's files into UserData/texture_replacements (texture_replacements = true in Config.toml; read at start).
+
+  tex1_128x128_ff0d42747046b66c_4d71081cc1d2542b_9  fight mash prompt "1"      -> south button (A / Cross)  = left punch
+  tex1_128x128_6150a782d87e506b_ef58c6d3a3c22c18_9  fight mash prompt "2"      -> east button (B / Circle)  = right punch
+  tex1_128x128_2a6f353beffd1d2c_5                   "Press A" icon              -> south button (A / Cross)
+  tex1_256x256_d256164176d768e4_ec6a3c79729529f9_9  controls screen: Wii Remote held sideways -> a gamepad (original art, same in both packs;
+                                                    drawn by tools/punchout_draw_gamepad.py)
+
+keyboard/ holds only the controls screen's picture (a keyboard, drawn by tools/punchout_draw_keyboard.py), used
+while the player is on the keyboard; its label then reads "Keyboard".
+
+The three prompts ("1", "2", "Press A") follow the player's controls: the port draws them at start, and again when
+the bindings or the device change, from the bound button's glyph (assets/glyphs, any button: bumpers and triggers
+too) or as a keycap for a key, at the sizes above (mash prompts 74%), over these files (punchout_prompts.cpp).
+
+Button glyphs: UI Elements by Arks @ScissorMarks, CC BY 4.0 (see assets/glyphs/CREDITS.txt). Controller art: made for
+this port. Replacements are 2x the original size.
+The controls screen's "Wii Remote" label reads "Gamepad": the port patches the player's own string table at start
+(runtime/src/hle/punchout_disc_patches.cpp; patched copy in UserData/Cache/disc_patches, nothing from the disc ships).
