+// Punch-Out!! front end (menus): which screen is up, which buttons it has, and controller navigation.
+//
+// Screens. The loaded-presentation list (manager *(u32*)0x80413AE0; first node = *(*(mgr+4)+4); node+0 =
+// presentation, node+4 = next; circular) is newest-first; popups are also on the modal stack *(u32*)0x80413AA0
+// (depth at +0x20, entry i at +i*8). A presentation is the screen's C++ object; +4 holds its path hash
+// (h = 0xFFFFFFFF; h = h*33 + lower(c) over "art/fe/<Name>", 801244BC; the same hash names FENL instances).
+//
+// Buttons. Screen objects embed 0x1C-byte button objects (base ctor 80041414, vtable 80323B30 and subclasses):
+//   +0 vtable, +4 byte 1, +8 FE instance (0 = none), +0xC state (0 off, 1 over, 2 down, 3 disabled),
+//   +0x10 button id (hash of e.g. "Nav_LeftButton", "CircuitSelectButton"), +0x14 sound set (+4 = Play_FE_Hover),
+//   +0x18 flags. OnEvent (vtable slot +0x14, 80041490) ignores everything while disabled.
+// An FE instance's children follow it in memory (Profile_Select tiles: the first Hit Region sits 0x1AF4 after the
+// instance), and every clickable has a child "Hit Region" (hash A45EB2A8): a unit box whose world matrix (flag word
+// at hash+0x60, 4x4 at hash+0x68) maps it straight to the pointer space: centre (m[12], -m[13]), size |m[0]| x |m[5]|
+// ([-1, 1] across the screen; pointer y down). Checked against the hover log on every menu.
